msgid "tipNoiseGaugeTitle"
msgstr "The noise gauge"

msgid "tipNoiseGaugeLine1"
msgstr "Every build, every recruit and every exploration makes noise, and your base makes a little every turn."

msgid "tipNoiseGaugeLine2"
msgstr "When the gauge reaches {threshold}, the monsters hear it: a raid is announced."

msgid "tipWorksitesTitle"
msgstr "Two builds per turn"

msgid "tipWorksitesLine1"
msgstr "Your HQ at level {level} opens a second build slot: two buildings go up each turn."

msgid "tipWorksitesLine2"
msgstr "HQ level {level} will open a third. Research stays at one per turn."

msgid "tipTechChoiceTitle"
msgstr "Research choices"

msgid "tipTechChoiceLine1"
msgstr "The next node of your branch is a choice between two options."

msgid "tipTechChoiceLine2"
msgstr "This choice is final: the other option stays closed for the whole game."

msgid "tipTechChoiceLine3"
msgstr "Take the time to read both before you start the research."

msgid "tipRaidAnnouncedTitle"
msgstr "A raid is coming"

msgid "tipRaidAnnouncedLine1"
msgstr "Your noise drew monsters: they will strike your base in {turns, plural, one{{turns} turn} other{{turns} turns}}."

msgid "tipRaidAnnouncedLine2"
msgstr "Recruit defenders: Harpooners are made for this."

msgid "tipRaidAnnouncedLine3"
msgstr "The rampart of the Coral Citadel will also help you hold."

msgid "tipRaidReportTitle"
msgstr "The raid report"

msgid "tipRaidReportLine1"
msgstr "After each raid, the report shows the fight, your losses and the loot."

msgid "tipRaidReportLine2"
msgstr "A lost raid plunders part of your resources."

msgid "tipRaidReportLine3"
msgstr "A repelled raid wipes out your losing streak."

msgid "tipLastChanceTitle"
msgstr "Last chance"

msgid "tipLastChanceLine1"
msgstr "{count, plural, one{Your base has lost {count} raid.} other{Your base has lost {count} raids in a row.}}"

msgid "tipLastChanceLine2"
msgstr "If the next raid is lost too, the game is over."

msgid "tipLastChanceLine3"
msgstr "Put your forces into defense: a victory wipes out the streak."

msgid "tipMonsterFamiliesTitle"
msgstr "Monster families"

msgid "tipMonsterFamiliesLine1"
msgstr "Each lair houses a family, with its own combat rule."

msgid "tipMonsterFamiliesLine2"
msgstr "Each family has a weak spot: a unit that counters it."

msgid "tipMonsterFamiliesLine3"
msgstr "Tap the lair on the Map to learn about it before you attack."

msgid "tipVolcanoWaveTitle"
msgstr "The Volcano's wave"

msgid "tipVolcanoWaveLine1"
msgstr "The Volcano sends its Krakens to take back the Core."

msgid "tipVolcanoWaveLine2"
msgstr "The wave strikes at the end of next turn: keep a garrison at the Core."

msgid "tipVolcanoWaveLine3"
msgstr "Each lost wave costs the Core a level."

msgid "tipLairTitle"
msgstr "Lairs"

msgid "tipLairLine1"
msgstr "On the Map, a monster lair guards its tile: attack it with your army."

msgid "tipLairLine2"
msgstr "Beaten monsters leave their loot, but every fight makes noise."

msgid "tipLairLine3"
msgstr "Check their numbers before you pick your units."

msgid "tipChestAndRuinsTitle"
msgstr "Chests and ruins"

msgid "tipChestAndRuinsLine1"
msgstr "A chest or ruins hide resources."

msgid "tipChestAndRuinsLine2"
msgstr "Tap the tile on the Map to search them: it's safe and silent."

msgid "tipTransitionBaseTitle"
msgstr "Transition bases"

msgid "tipTransitionBaseLine1"
msgstr "A guarded base on the Map leads to the depths."

msgid "tipTransitionBaseLine2"
msgstr "Once you storm it, it brings you pearls every turn."

msgid "tipTransitionBaseLine3"
msgstr "It also opens the way to the next level."

msgid "tipDescentTitle"
msgstr "The descent"

msgid "tipDescentLine1"
msgstr "Your Descent Module sends units to the level below, through the Rift."

msgid "tipDescentLine2"
msgstr "Careful: a unit sent down never comes back up."

msgid "tipDescentLine3"
msgstr "Down there, more lairs await you, and the road to the Core."

msgid "tipEventsTitle"
msgstr "Events"

msgid "tipEventsLine1"
msgstr "Every {minGap} to {maxGap} turns, an event shakes the abyss."

msgid "tipEventsLine2"
msgstr "You have the next turn to choose your answer on its card."

msgid "tipEventsLine3"
msgstr "If you don't choose, the cautious option applies automatically."

msgid "tipWarmCurrentLine1"
msgstr "A warm current boosts your production for {turns, plural, one{{turns} turn} other{{turns} turns}}."

msgid "tipWarmCurrentLine2"
msgstr "But its swirl makes noise every turn."

msgid "tipWarmCurrentLine3"
msgstr "Make the most of it if your defenses are ready for a raid."

msgid "tipWreckLine1"
msgstr "A sunken galleon stays {turns, plural, one{{turns} turn} other{{turns} turns}} at the edge of the explored area."

msgid "tipWreckLine2"
msgstr "Explore its tile with a Scout, then search it for its loot."

msgid "tipWreckLine3"
msgstr "Searching makes noise (+{noise}): pick your moment."

msgid "tipPredatorsLine1"
msgstr "A great shark and its shoal prowl around your base."

msgid "tipPredatorsLine2"
msgstr "Fight them for their loot, or give up algae to drive them away."

msgid "tipPredatorsLine3"
msgstr "Losing to them never ends the game."

msgid "tipStormLine1"
msgstr "The storm closes exploration for {turns, plural, one{{turns} turn} other{{turns} turns}}."

msgid "tipStormLine2"
msgstr "In return, it covers your noise: the gauge drops by {relief}."

msgid "tipSurvivorsLine1"
msgstr "A stranded capsule shelters survivors."

msgid "tipSurvivorsLine2"
msgstr "Taken in, they join your base as Harpooners."

msgid "tipSurvivorsLine3"
msgstr "Like the rest of your army, they eat algae every turn."

msgid "tipCaravanLine1"
msgstr "A turtle caravan passes near your base."

msgid "tipCaravanLine2"
msgstr "Its merchant crab trades your most plentiful resource for the scarcest one."

msgid "tipColdCurrentLine1"
msgstr "A cold current slows your algae for {turns, plural, one{{turns} turn} other{{turns} turns}}."

msgid "tipColdCurrentLine2"
msgstr "Heating the greenhouses costs energy, but saves the harvest."

msgid "tipColdCurrentLine3"
msgstr "Without algae, your army can't hold out: watch your stock."

msgid "guideLessonHqLevel1"
msgstr "Welcome to the abyss! Tap the HQ to start your first build: just one per turn to begin with. Then press “Next turn”."

msgid "guideLessonAlgaeFarm"
msgstr "Well done on your first build! Algae feed your army: every unit eats some each turn. Build the Algae Farm."

msgid "guideLessonMines"
msgstr "Coral and ore pay for almost everything. Build the Coral Mine, then the Ore Extractor, one per turn. Look closely: each level costs more than the one before."

msgid "guideLessonSolarPanel"
msgstr "The Extractor uses energy, and the Barracks will too. Without energy, they stop. Build the Solar Panel."

msgid "guideLessonSolarPanelLevel2"
msgstr "Energy runs out fast: every new building draws on it, and research will too. Raise the Solar Panel to level 2 before starting research."

msgid "guideLessonHqLevel2"
msgstr "HQ level {level} unlocks the Barracks and the Laboratory. But every build makes noise: watch the gauge at the top of the screen, it draws monsters."

msgid "guideLessonBarracksAndScouts"
msgstr "Build the Barracks, then recruit {count, plural, one{{count} Scout} other{{count} Scouts}} in the Army tab. Every unit eats algae each turn, and every recruit raises the noise."

msgid "guideLessonExplore"
msgstr "Around your base, everything is in the fog. On the Map, send a Scout to a nearby tile: you'll find monster lairs of different families there, and sometimes chests."

msgid "guideLessonLaboratoryAndResearch"
msgstr "Build the Laboratory, open a branch in the Tech tab and start a research project. Only one research per turn, and some choices are final: take the time to read."

msgid "guideLessonFirstRaid"
msgstr "Noise always ends up drawing a raid, announced {turns, plural, one{{turns} turn} other{{turns} turns}} ahead. Recruit Harpooners to defend your base. Later, the Citadel's rampart will help you too."

msgid "guideGoalMet"
msgstr "Well done, that's it! End the turn to complete the objective and collect your reward."

msgid "guideWorksiteTaken"
msgstr "Your build for this turn is already taken. End the turn: you'll build the next one next turn."

msgid "guideAlreadyRecruited"
msgstr "You've already recruited these units this turn. End the turn to recruit more."

msgid "guideExploring"
msgstr "Your Scout is on its way. End the turn to find out what the tile hides."

msgid "guideStorm"
msgstr "A storm closes exploration until the end of turn {turn}. Be patient: the objective will wait, end the turn."

msgid "guideWreckWithoutBarracks"
msgstr "A wreck has sunk near your base, visible until the end of turn {turn}. Reaching it takes a Scout, so the Barracks: keep going with your objective, they will come."

msgid "guideWreckWithoutScout"
msgstr "A wreck has sunk near your base, visible until the end of turn {turn}. Recruit a Scout in the Army tab to go and search it."

msgid "guideRaidIntro"
msgstr "The raid arrives on turn {turn} with {monsters, plural, one{{monsters} monster} other{{monsters} monsters}}."

msgid "guideRaidOutOfReach"
msgstr "Recruit as many Harpooners as you can in the Army tab."

msgid "guideRaidHeld"
msgstr "Your defense should repel it: end the turn to wait for it."

msgid "guideRaidNeeded"
msgstr "Have at least {needed, plural, one{{needed} Harpooner} other{{needed} Harpooners}} on level 1: you're {missing} short."

msgid "guideRaidRecruitNow"
msgstr "{missing, plural, one{Recruit it in the Army tab.} other{Recruit them in the Army tab.}}"

msgid "guideRaidRecruitNextTurn"
msgstr "You've already recruited this turn: recruit {missing, plural, one{it} other{them}} next turn."

msgid "guideRaidHoldOn"
msgstr "You've already recruited this turn: end it and hold on."

msgid "guideAdmiralNeedsBarracks"
msgstr "To take {post, select, faille{a Rift} cheminee{a Vent} other{the Core}}, you need an Admiral. Raise the Barracks to level {level}."

msgid "guideAdmiralToRecruit"
msgstr "Recruit an Admiral: he doesn't fight, but without him {post, select, faille{the Rift} cheminee{the Vent} other{the Core}} can't be taken."

msgid "guideAdmiralToSend"
msgstr "To take {post, select, faille{the Rift} cheminee{the Vent} other{the Core}}, your Admiral must go down to level {level}. He is on level {from}: send him through your {passage, select, faille{Rift} other{Vent}}, highlighted on the Map on level {from}."

msgid "guidePostToFind"
msgstr "{post, select, faille{Explore the Map to find a Rift, but don't forget to keep upgrading your buildings and your army!} cheminee{Explore the Map on level 2 to find a Vent, but don't forget to keep upgrading your buildings and your army!} other{Explore the Map on level 3 to find the Core, but don't forget to keep upgrading your buildings and your army!}}"

msgid "guidePostAssault"
msgstr "{post, select, faille{A Rift} cheminee{A Vent} other{The Core}}! Your Admiral must survive: cover him with Guardians."

msgid "guidePostAssaultArmy"
msgstr "{count, plural, =0{Your escort is enough} one{Send him with at least {count} Harpooner} other{Send him with at least {count} Harpooners}}: you win {wins} times out of {rehearsals}."

msgid "guideAdmiralFell"
msgstr "Victory, but your Admiral fell: {post, select, faille{the Rift} cheminee{the Vent} other{the Core}} is not taken. Cover him with Guardians and try again."

msgid "guidePassageNeedsHq"
msgstr "{passage, select, descentModule{The Descent Module} other{The Pressure Capsule}} needs Headquarters level {level}. Raise your Headquarters first."

msgid "guidePostUndefended"
msgstr "{post, select, faille{Your Rift is guarded only by your units on level {level}. If it falls, your Module is destroyed} other{Your Vent is guarded only by your units on level {level}. If it falls, your Capsule is destroyed}} and your units down there are lost."

msgid "guideKernelWaveNeeded"
msgstr "The Krakens are coming to take the Core back! Put at least {needed, plural, one{{needed} unit} other{{needed} units}} in the garrison before the end of the turn, or the Core loses a level."

msgid "guideKernelWaveAll"
msgstr "{monsters} Krakens are coming to take the Core back! Garrison every unit you can before the end of the turn, or the Core loses a level."

msgid "guideLessonDescentModule"
msgstr "Build the Descent Module: it opens your Rift down to level 2."

msgid "guideLessonDescendLevel2"
msgstr "Send units down to level 2 through the Rift. Careful: they never come back up."

msgid "guideLessonHqLevel8"
msgstr "The Pressure Capsule, which leads to level 3, needs Headquarters level 8. Raise your Headquarters."

msgid "guideLessonPressureCapsule"
msgstr "Build the Pressure Capsule: it opens your Vent down to level 3."

msgid "guideLessonDescendLevel3"
msgstr "Send units down to level 3 through the Vent. Careful: they never come back up."

msgid "guideLessonHqLevel10"
msgstr "Headquarters level 10 will let you garrison units in the Core once it is taken. Raise your Headquarters."

msgid "guideLessonKernelLevel1"
msgstr "The Core is yours! Build it to level 1: Kraken waves will come, and only its garrison will defend it."

