msgid "tipAdmiralTitle"
msgstr "The Admiral"

msgid "tipAdmiralLine1"
msgstr "The Abyss Admiral does not fight: he leads the assault."

msgid "tipAdmiralLine2"
msgstr "A Rift, a Vent or the Core is taken only if he survives the assault."

msgid "tipAdmiralLine3"
msgstr "Cover him with Guardians: they draw the blows in his place."

msgid "tipPostDefenceTitle"
msgstr "Defending your posts"

msgid "tipPostDefenceLine1"
msgstr "Only your units on the level below defend a post."

msgid "tipPostDefenceLine2"
msgstr "Factions attack your posts without warning."

msgid "tipPostDefenceLine3"
msgstr "If it falls, your Descent Module (or Capsule) is destroyed and your units down there are lost."

msgid "tipKernelGarrisonTitle"
msgstr "The Core's garrison"

msgid "tipKernelGarrisonLine1"
msgstr "Against the Krakens, only the garrison defends the Core."

msgid "tipKernelGarrisonLine2"
msgstr "Your units left outside, on level {level}, do not fight."

msgid "tipKernelGarrisonLine3"
msgstr "Move them in with \"{action}\", on the Core's sheet."

msgid "tipPostLostTitle"
msgstr "Post lost"

msgid "tipPostLostLine1"
msgstr "Your post fell: its Module or Capsule is destroyed and your units down there are lost."

msgid "tipPostLostLine2"
msgstr "The winner now holds the post."

msgid "tipPostLostLine3"
msgstr "To take it back, lead a new assault with an Abyss Admiral."

msgid "tipAbyssListensTitle"
msgstr "The abyss listens"

msgid "tipAbyssListensLine1"
msgstr "In the water, everything carries: a worksite, a recruit, a fight, even a sleeping dome."

msgid "tipAbyssListensLine2"
msgstr "When the noise goes beyond what the Trench tolerates, its creatures rise in turn."

msgid "tipAbyssListensLine3"
msgstr "A dome that loses three raids in a row goes dark: only the Trench puts a dome out."

msgid "tipRivalColoniesTitle"
msgstr "The rival colonies"

msgid "tipRivalColoniesLine1"
msgstr "The other ships of the Sinking settled on the same day as you."

msgid "tipRivalColoniesLine2"
msgstr "Each dome kept the habits of its crew: freebooters, monks, smiths, pilgrims…"

msgid "tipRivalColoniesLine3"
msgstr "They all know the promise of the Core, and they all race toward the Volcano."

msgid "tipAncientsTitle"
msgstr "The Ancients and their pearls"

msgid "tipAncientsLine1"
msgstr "Before the Sinking, the Ancients lived in the Trench: they left its ruins, its passages and the Core."

msgid "tipAncientsLine2"
msgstr "Pearls are born where the Volcano's fire meets the cold, and they once opened their machines."

msgid "tipAncientsLine3"
msgstr "A passage of the Ancients must be claimed: that is why it takes an Admiral."

msgid "tipForgeTowersTitle"
msgstr "The forge-towers"

msgid "tipForgeTowersLine1"
msgstr "Beneath the reef, daylight ends: the Colossi sleep there, in the ruins of the Ancients."

msgid "tipForgeTowersLine2"
msgstr "The Vents are their forge-towers, and their magma golems have gone wild again."

msgid "tipForgeTowersLine3"
msgstr "A volcanic Titan keeps watch atop each one, one eye open on the dark."

msgid "tipAwakeningTitle"
msgstr "The awakening"

msgid "tipAwakeningLine1"
msgstr "The captured Core is only a cold forge: it must be rekindled fire after fire, ten in all."

msgid "tipAwakeningLine2"
msgstr "Each fire drives the Kraken out of the magma chambers, and it rises to coil around the Core."

msgid "tipAwakeningLine3"
msgstr "At the tenth fire, the heat rises all the way to the reef: the Volcano is tamed."

msgid "leviathanAttackerName"
msgstr "The Leviathan"

msgid "leviathanBannerTitle"
msgstr "Counter-attack on the Rift at the end of the turn"

msgid "leviathanBannerForce"
msgstr "Leviathan + {sentinels} Sentinels · level {level} defenders: {count}"

msgid "leviathanDueWarning"
msgstr "The Leviathan strikes your Rift at the end of the turn, and {count, plural, =0{no defender awaits it} one{only {count} defender awaits it} other{only {count} defenders await it}} on level {level}."

msgid "guideLeviathanReturn"
msgstr "The Leviathan is coming back to take its Rift! Only your units on level {level} defend it. If it falls, your Module is destroyed and your units down there are lost."

msgid "guideLeviathanReinforce"
msgstr "Send {count, plural, one{{count} more Harpooner} other{{count} more Harpooners}}."

